Z||000000||I'mSmall||11-01-2001||10:24 AM||||I just want to know if the radiator for the 4 cylinder is the same for the V6. I bought my 86 that has a V6 with a 4 cylinder V.I.N. with over heating problems. The person said that it might be the water pump, she also said it started over heating after she had the radiator replaced. Since buying it I have replaced the water pump, the coolant relay, the fan switch, thermostat, radiator cap, thermostat housing cap, and all of the hoses. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||11-01-2001||01:07 PM||||If it started overheating right after she got the radiator replaced, the cooling system probably has a lot of air in it.   Most shops don't know that there is a special filling procedure unique to Fieros, and if it is not followed a lot of air can get into it.  You can "burp" the system yourself, but I dont know the procedure.  Try a search for it under the technical section, I know that there have been a few threads in the past.||||reg||1
